&nbsp;

<b>Characterization Labels</b>

<b>Ancap.</b> This label implies ancap only. The group self-identifies as ancap and has standards (formal or informal) whereby it consciously chooses others. NB: Ancap always represents a spectrum of views and even in such a community there will still be a spectrum of views. Also, the center of this spectrum may be anywhere from the larger spectrum of all ancapper views. Caution is indicated.

<b>Friends.</b> This is a mixed grouping of ancappers and ancap friendlies. The mixture here can be much less stable and the ancappers may form only a limited minority. Who or what the friends may be is also dependent on personal perspective. One ancapper's friends may be seen by another as enemies. Caution!

<b>Mixed.</b> Ancapers are present in greater number than is seen as normal in the surrounding society. They may or may not be organized, know each other, or be living openly or demonstrably as ancappers.

&nbsp;

